","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:737-741 — `if \"token\" in record: raise AuthConfigError(... use 'token_sha256' or 'token_env')`","src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:749-757 — record must have EXACTLY ONE of token_sha256 (64-char hex) or token_env","src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:198-207 — verifier 'stores ONLY SHA-256 hex digests (never the plaintext tokens)'","Plan AC quote: 'the materialized file contains it (the file is NOT under the rsync'd tree)' and 'the static verifier accepts a request bearing a materialized PAT ... through the real read path'"],"finding":"The materialization AC mis-states the consumer contract of the file it targets: the `static` verifier's tokens file (parsed by `_load_static_tokens`/`_parse_static_record`) stores ONLY `token_sha256` hex digests or `token_env` references and raises `AuthConfigError` on any plaintext `token` field, yet the AC asserts fetch-secrets.sh 'materializes the PAT file from SSM into the on-box location the static verifier reads' and that 'the materialized file contains it [the known PAT value]'. The plan does not specify the required SSM-value -> tokens-file transform (hash the SSM PAT to a 64-char SHA-256 digest and emit a `token_sha256` record, OR materialize the PAT into a 0600 env file and emit a `token_env` record), so as written the materialized file would be rejected by the very verifier it feeds.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faf9dde51d2c7ffee","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — materialize + verifier oracles","norm_id":"n6e234345c2224872","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["fetch-secrets.sh writes the raw SSM PAT into tokens.json -> _load_static_tokens raises AuthConfigError at verifier __init__ -> rebar-mcp fails to start","The 'materialize' oracle asserts the file contains the raw PAT value, which would only pass against a file the real verifier cannot load"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Per client, hash the SSM-fetched PAT to its 64-char SHA-256 hex and emit `{\"tokens\":[{\"name\":\"copilot\",\"client_id\":\"copilot\",\"scopes\":[...],\"token_sha256\":\"<hex>\"}, ...]}` to the gitignored on-box tokens file (0600, atomic mktemp+chmod+mv, matching the opcert/rebar-bot-signing-key precedent). Update the materialize oracle to assert the file contains the digest of the known PAT (not the PAT), and keep the verifier-contrast oracle presenting the raw PAT in the Authorization header.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the SSM-value -> tokens-file transform: state whether fetch-secrets.sh (a) hashes each per-client PAT to a 64-char `token_sha256` and emits the `{\"tokens\":[...]}` JSON the verifier reads, or (b) materializes each PAT into a 0600 env source and the tokens JSON references it via `token_env` — and reconcile the AC materialize oracle ('the materialized file contains [the PAT value]') with the verifier's plaintext-token rejection.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:737-741 rejects a plaintext 'token' field: 'carries a plaintext token field — use token_sha256 or token_env'","src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:749-768: EXACTLY ONE of token_sha256 (64-char hex) or token_env; token_env reads the token from an env var and hashes it","fetch-secrets.sh:141-158 writes .env env values; :103-132 materializes signing keys to 0600 files — two distinct sinks, neither producing the tokens JSON as described","AC materialize oracle: 'the materialized file contains it' (the known PAT value) is inconsistent with the digest/env-ref-only tokens file if 'the file' is the tokens file the verifier reads"],"finding":"The plan's materialization mechanism conflates delivering the raw PAT value with the tokens file the `static` verifier actually reads; the verifier's parser (`_parse_static_record`) requires each record to be JSON with EXACTLY ONE of `token_sha256` (64-hex digest) or `token_env` (env var name) and REJECTS any file containing a plaintext `token`. A file that literally 'contains' the PAT value is not loadable by the verifier. The plan does not specify the SSM-value -> tokens-file transform.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f00704cac416b57be","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach bullets ('the static verifier's accepted-token set is sourced from those materialized secrets') + AC materialize oracle ('the materialized file contains it')","norm_id":"n31ed16de45d62b74","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer materializes a file of raw PATs at the verifier's tokens_file path; verifier raises AuthConfigError on plaintext 'token' or 'not valid JSON' at __init__ and rebar-mcp fails to start","Test asserts the materialized file contains the known value, but the verifier-contrast test needs a valid JSON tokens file — the two oracles describe incompatible artifacts"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State that fetch-secrets.sh emits the on-box `mcp.auth_static_tokens_file` JSON with one record per client (name/client_id/scopes) carrying `token_sha256 = sha256(PAT)` computed from the SSM value (never a plaintext token), matching `_parse_static_record`; the materialize oracle then asserts the record's digest equals sha256(known-PAT), not that the file contains the raw value.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the SSM-value -> tokens-file transform against the real read path: state whether fetch-secrets.sh hashes each per-client PAT to a 64-char token_sha256 JSON record, or writes each PAT to a 0600 env source and emits a token_env-referencing record — and correct the materialize AC away from 'the file contains the raw value' toward the schema _parse_static_record actually accepts.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:737-741 — a plaintext 'token' field -> AuthConfigError('use token_sha256 or token_env')","src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:749-770 — a record must have EXACTLY ONE of token_sha256 (64-hex) or token_env; token_env reads+hashes at load","Plan AC: 'a stubbed SSM/aws sink feeding a known value -> the materialized file contains it' — a plaintext-value assertion at odds with the schema","Classification: Partially-verified — the SSM CLI + materialize-to-file integration exists and is used, but the specific PAT->tokens-file surface transform is unconfirmed/unspecified"],"finding":"The materialization AC asserts the on-box file 'contains' the raw SSM PAT value, but the actual consumer the plan names (StaticBearerVerifier -> _load_static_tokens/_parse_static_record) rejects any plaintext token: each record must carry token_sha256 (64-char hex) or token_env, and a 'token' field raises AuthConfigError. The transform from the raw SSM PAT to the verifier's accepted file schema is unspecified, so the integration as described is not achievable without a named transform step.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7a5b4a51dfe3b5d5","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — materialize oracle ('the materialized file contains it'); Approach bullet 'the static verifier's accepted-token set is sourced from those materialized secrets'","norm_id":"n8a92dd2c83c60f0f","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["fetch-secrets.sh writes the raw PAT into the tokens file; the verifier's _parse_static_record rejects it at __init__ and rebar-mcp refuses to start","The test 'materializes -> file contains the known value' passes while the real verifier read path would reject that same file"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Have fetch-secrets.sh emit the on-box tokens file as {\"tokens\":[{\"name\":..., \"client_id\":..., \"scopes\":[...], \"token_sha256\":\"<sha256 of the SSM PAT>\"}, ...]} (or materialize each PAT to a 0600 file/env and reference via token_env), matching _parse_static_record; rewrite the materialize oracle to assert the record's token_sha256 equals sha256(known value) rather than that the file contains the plaintext value.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the concrete SSM param name pattern (e.g. /rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-<client>) and the exact on-box materialized file path the static verifier reads, so materialization target and verifier read path are pinned to the same location.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Terraform SSM params for the per-client PATs (one per client: copilot/codex/claude) under the existing /rebar/prod/ prefix'","'materializes the PAT file from SSM into the on-box location the static verifier reads'"],"finding":"The exact SSM parameter names and the concrete on-box materialized file path are not fully pinned — the plan gives the prefix (/rebar/prod/) and the client set (copilot/codex/claude) but not the full param-name pattern, and describes the materialized path only relationally ('the on-box location the static verifier reads').","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb35374e273e651ae","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach bullet 1 + Acceptance Criteria (materialize oracle)","norm_id":"n6eccd0af582b9f8c","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor must invent the exact param name (e.g. /rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-copilot) and the on-box destination path, risking a mismatch with what the static verifier's _load_static_tokens actually reads."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify fetch-secrets.sh error behavior when the PAT SSM param is missing/empty/unreachable (fail the deploy loudly, or surface a clear error) so an empty tokens file never silently reaches the static verifier's __init__.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b","T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.548,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'fetch-secrets.sh wiring to materialize them on the box' and 'The static verifier's accepted-token set is sourced from those materialized secrets.'","No error-handling clause for a missing/empty SSM param; the verifier loads its token set ONCE at __init__, so an empty file at init silently yields an accept-nothing verifier with no surfaced error."],"finding":"The plan does not specify how fetch-secrets.sh behaves when the per-client PAT SSM param is missing, empty, or unreachable at deploy time — whether it fails loudly or silently materializes an empty/partial tokens file that the static verifier then loads (rejecting all clients, or worse).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0eed8af32b897045","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach + rationale / AC 'fetch-secrets.sh materializes the PAT file from SSM'","norm_id":"nd836678c0628a7d6","priority":0.402,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An SSM param is not yet created (additive rollout) or was deleted during rollback: fetch materializes an empty file, rebar-mcp starts, and every client 401s with no operator-visible cause.","A transient SSM/aws fetch failure leaves a stale or empty file and the deploy proceeds silently."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add an AC that the materialization step errors non-zero (and does not overwrite an existing good file) when the SSM param is absent or empty, and add a verifier test for the empty/missing-file read path.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_w